# qa/dep-wall.ledger — THE DEPENDENCY WALL, pinned at the measurement it was armed at (Law 9).
# Read by `cargo xtask gate dep-wall` (xtask/src/gates/dep_wall.rs):
# no plugin closure carries a socket or TLS stack of its own; every plugin reaches the network through
# a need and the connector does the rest (DECISIONS #40(a); THE DESIGN: connections).
#
# DRAIN-ONLY, CHECKED BOTH WAYS: a measured `crate<TAB>offender` this file does not pin is RED (a new
# offender — never pinned in the change that introduced it), and a line the tree no longer measures is
# RED (strike it in the commit that drained it). It reaches zero when the coexistence window closes,
# and this file is deleted then.
#
# A transport CARRIER, whose whole job is the socket, is exempt by its declared KIND (`transport`),
# never by a row here: a `carrier<TAB>crate` row is refused. The connector is a cleanliness crate and
# never in scope.
busbar-llm	hyper-util
busbar-llm	reqwest
busbar-llm	rustls
busbar-llm	socket2
busbar-llm	tokio (net)
busbar-llm	tokio-rustls
